rsions\n\nReproducible in: 4.4-stable, 4.4.1-stable, 4.5-dev2\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Linux Mint 21.3 (Virginia) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU - AMD Ryzen 7 8845HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads); Godot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-11600KF @ 3.90GHz (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nDictionary, that is statically typed to have Node as its key, will break upon freeing any Node that is a key in the dictionary.\nSeems to break (or become unreliable) as a whole, but was found while trying to inspect a Node that had aforementioned type of dictionary as a property. So it might be just an inspector issue?\n\nFrom personal observations:\nAny kind of Node works.\nDoesn't happen if the Node is a value, and isn't a key.\nValue breaks when the key does. (In the MRP: upon trying to print the dictionary, returns `{ <Freed Object>: 0 }`, even though initially the int assigned was 1 and not 0)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAbstractly:\n1. Create dictionary, such as: `var dictionary_name : Dictionary[Node, int]`.\n2. Add an entry to the dictionary.\n3. Free the Node used in entry.\n4. Try \"remotely\" inspecting the node containing the dictionary.\n\nMRP:\n1. Run project.\n2. Go to Remote Scene Inspector.\n3. Inspect (press) Main.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[exampleDictionaryIssueProject.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19765709/exampleDictionaryIssueProject.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","followin